; The dev profile's JavaScript without source maps or pretty-printing: they
; made each library's JavaScript a third slower to compile, the dev
; main.bc.js twice as large (64 MB), and every page load and test parse it.
; (sourcemap no) covers linking only: dune still asks for inline maps when it
; compiles each library, which --no-source-map (given after) overrides.
; To debug in a browser with them: dune build --profile debug-js.

(env
 (dev
  (js_of_ocaml
   (sourcemap no)
   (flags
    ((:standard \ --pretty)
     --no-source-map))))
 (debug-js
  (js_of_ocaml
   (sourcemap inline))))

; The slow tier: tests that run only with PRIGH_TEST_TIER=full (`./test
; --full`), by (enabled_if (= %{env:PRIGH_TEST_TIER=default} full)) on their
; inline_tests, cram or rule stanzas. Their code builds in every run.
